<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.AFRICA MAIZE CHIEF TO WIND DOWN BOARD'S BUSINESS.</title>
<headline>S.AFRICA MAIZE CHIEF TO WIND DOWN BOARD'S BUSINESS.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The South African Maize Board has appointed Leon du Plessis, the current chief executive, to wind down the matters of the board, Agriculture and Land Affairs Minister Derek Hanekom said on Monday.</p>
<p>Hanekom said in a statement du Plessis is to be contracted by the board for the period May 1 to October 31, or until a liquidator has been appointed in terms of the Marketing of Agricultural Products Bill.</p>
<p>The Bill, passed by parliament last year, outlaws statutory agricultural market controls and signals the demise of all commodity control boards by the beginning of 1998.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
